diff --git a/docs/bots.md b/docs/bots.md
index 1b1233a..4069dc5 100644
--- a/docs/bots.md
+++ b/docs/bots.md
@@ -48,3 +48,30 @@ Bots are chat members that post messages via HTTP API. They can be members of ro
 - Top-level `GET /messages/:id` fixed to support Location header: `MessagesController#set_room` derives room from message when `room_id` missing, ensuring membership.
 - Human tokens (nil or manually set) cannot post (scoped to bots).
 - Avatar optional, name required (model validation + HTML required).
+
+## Webhooks (mention callbacks)
+
+- Column `users.webhook_url` (string, nullable, aliased as `bot_webhook_url`) — optional per-bot callback URL.
+  - Normalized via `normalizes :webhook_url, with: ->(url) { url.to_s.strip.presence }` so empty/whitespace form input becomes `nil` (removes webhook).
+  - Validated as HTTP(S) URL with host when present (`URI::HTTP`, allows localhost/private for dev/test bots; no `PrivateNetworkGuard` block so local bot servers work in QA).
+  - Scope `User.with_webhook` (`where.not(webhook_url: [nil, ""])`), helper `webhook_enabled?`.
+- Form (`_form` shared by `/bots/new` + edit): adds optional `url_field :webhook_url` with label/placeholder/aria-label + visible text exactly "Webhook URL" (QA drives by label). No `required`. Permitted in `BotsController#bot_params`. `update` now renders `:edit` on validation failure (like `create`) instead of `update!` 500.
+- Autocomplete: no change needed — `Autocompletable::UsersController` uses `User.active` / `room.users` which already include bots (verified: bots auto-join opens, can be added to closeds via `User.active.ordered` member UIs, appear in both global + room-scoped JSON).
+- Trigger: `Room#receive` (called via `Message.after_create_commit`) now also `Room::BotMentionJob.perform_later(room, message)` — async so posting never waits on bot HTTP (queue adapters: `:test` in test, `:async` in dev, `:resque` in prod).
+  - Job finds `message.mentionees.bots.active.with_webhook.where.not(id: message.creator_id)` — only member bots with webhooks, excludes self-mention to avoid bot triggering itself. Each bot handled independently with per-bot rescue + continue.
+  - `Room::BotWebhookNotifier(room:, message:, bot:)` builds payload + POSTs + handles sync reply. Follows `Room::MessagePusher` / `PushMessageJob` pattern.
+- Payload (`Content-Type: application/json`, relative paths so bot knows its Campfire origin):
+  ```json
+  { "event": "mention", "author": {"id","name"}, "room": {"id","name","reply_to": "/rooms/:id/:bot_token/messages"}, "message": {"id","body": {"text","html"}, "link": "/rooms/:id/@:msg_id"} }
+  ```
+  - `text`: `plain_text_body` with bot's own `"@#{bot.name}"` stripped (`gsub` literal + strip + collapse spaces, preserves newlines) so each bot sees command addressed to it (multi-bot: each keeps other bots' mentions).
+  - `html`: `message.body.to_s` (full `<div class="trix-content">…</div>` including mention attachments).
+  - `reply_to`: `room_bot_messages_path(room.id, bot.bot_token)` — bot's own async posting URL for that room.
+  - `link`: `room_at_message_path(room, message)` — deep link `/rooms/:id/@:msg_id` scrolling to message.
+- Sync reply handling in notifier:
+  - `POST` via `Net::HTTP` (open 5s, read 10s), no redirect/SSRF guard, `rescue` + warn on any network/URI error (job never retries/crashes).
+  - `200` + `text/plain`/`text/html` (case-insensitive substring, blank treated as plain) with non-blank scrubbed body → `room.messages.create!(creator: bot, body:)` + `broadcast_create` (membership re-checked, like `BotMessagesController`). Other `200` types ignored.
+  - `204` → no message. Other statuses → log + ignore.
+  - Bot reply goes through same `broadcast_create` + `room.receive` (unread/push/mention) as async posts.
+- Async reply: bot `POST`s raw body to `reply_to` later (existing `Rooms::BotMessagesController`, 201/422/404/401).
+- Edge: deleted room/message before job → `discard_on DeserializationError` + `rescue RecordNotFound`; webhook removed before job → `return unless webhook_url.present?`; bot removed from room before sync reply → skip post; network timeout/500/invalid URL → warn, no message, no retry.
